{"sataBisaj": [{"id": "SataBizaj", "headword": "शतभिषज्", "headword_slp1": "SataBizaj", "fold": "sataBisaj", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "23. Śatabhiṣaj or Śatabhiṣa, ‘having a hundred physicians,’ seems to be Aquarii with the others around it vaguely conceived as numbering a hundred.\n24, 25. proṣṭha-padās (fem. plur.), ‘feet of a stool,’ or later bhadra-padās, ‘auspicious feet,’ a double asterism forming a square, the former (pūrva) consisting of and Pegasi, the latter (uttara) of Pegasi and Andromedæ.\nFoot notes So probably in Maitrāyaṇī Saṃhitā, ii. 13, 20, where see von Schroeder's critical note. The Śāntikalpa, 5, and Nakṣatrakalpa, 2, have Śatabhiṣā, and the latter, 1, has Śatabhiṣa (masculine).\nŚāntikalpa, 5, etc.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["shatabhiShaj", "shatabhiShaj_23", "śatabhiṣaj", "śatabhiṣaj_23", "शतभिषज्", "శతభిషజ్", "శతభిషజ్_౨౩", "ಶತಭಿಷಜ್", "ಶತಭಿಷಜ್_೨೩"], "synonyms_slp1": ["shatabhiShaj", "shatabhiShaj_23", "śatabhiṣaj", "śatabhiṣaj_23", "SataBizaj", "శతభిషజ్", "శతభిషజ్_౨౩", "ಶತಭಿಷಜ್", "ಶತಭಿಷಜ್_೨೩"]}], "sata-dyumna": [{"id": "Sata-dyumna", "headword": "शत-द्युम्न", "headword_slp1": "Sata-dyumna", "fold": "sata-dyumna", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Śata-dyumna (‘possessing a hundred glories’) is the name of a man who, along with yajñeṣu, was made prosperous by the priest mātsya through his knowledge of the exact moment for sacrifice, according to the taittirīya brāhmaṇa (i. 5, 2, 1).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["dyumna", "shata", "shata-dyumna", "shatadyumna", "śata", "śata-dyumna", "śatadyumna", "द्युम्न", "शत", "शतद्युम्न", "ద్యుమ్న", "శత", "శత-ద్యుమ్న", "శతద్యుమ్న", "ದ್ಯುಮ್ನ", "ಶತ", "ಶತ-ದ್ಯುಮ್ನ", "ಶತದ್ಯುಮ್ನ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dyumna", "shata", "shata-dyumna", "shatadyumna", "śata", "śata-dyumna", "śatadyumna", "dyumna", "Sata", "Satadyumna", "ద్యుమ్న", "శత", "శత-ద్యుమ్న", "శతద్యుమ్న", "ದ್ಯುಮ್ನ", "ಶತ", "ಶತ-ದ್ಯುಮ್ನ", "ಶತದ್ಯುಮ್ನ"]}], "sata-pati": [{"id": "Sata-pati", "headword": "शत-पति", "headword_slp1": "Sata-pati", "fold": "sata-pati", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Śata-pati occurs in a verse of the Maitrāyaṇī Saṃhitā and the taittirīya brāhmaṇa as an epithet of indra, who is described as alone the ‘lord of a hundred’ among men. To interpret the expression as ‘lord of a hundred gods,’ as does the commentary on the taittirīya brāhmaṇa, is obviously impossible. It seems clear that there is a reference to an analogous human functionary--viz., the lord of a hundred villages, known in the later law --who was probably at once a judicial deputy of the sovereign and a revenue collector, an ancient magistrate and collector.\nFoot notes iv. 14, 12.\nii. 8, 4, 2.\nSee Foy, Die ko7nigliche Gewalt, 74.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["pati", "shata", "shata-pati", "shatapati", "śata", "śata-pati", "śatapati", "पति", "शत", "शतपति", "పతి", "శత", "శత-పతి", "శతపతి", "ಪತಿ", "ಶತ", "ಶತ-ಪತಿ", "ಶತಪತಿ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["pati", "shata", "shata-pati", "shatapati", "śata", "śata-pati", "śatapati", "pati", "Sata", "Satapati", "పతి", "శత", "శత-పతి", "శతపతి", "ಪತಿ", "ಶತ", "ಶತ-ಪತಿ", "ಶತಪತಿ"]}], "sata-balaksa mOdgalya": [{"id": "Sata-balAkza mOdgalya", "headword": "शत-बलाक्ष मौद्गल्य", "headword_slp1": "Sata-balAkza mOdgalya", "fold": "sata-balaksa mOdgalya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Śata-balākṣa Maudgalya (‘descendant of mudgala’) is the name of a grammarian in the nirukta (xi. 6).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["balaakSha maudgalya", "balaaxa maudgalya", "balākṣa maudgalya", "shata", "shata-balaakSha maudgalya", "shata-balaaxa maudgalya", "shatabalaakSha maudgalya", "shatabalaaxa maudgalya", "śata", "śata-balākṣa maudgalya", "śatabalākṣa maudgalya", "बलाक्ष मौद्गल्य", "शत", "शतबलाक्ष मौद्गल्य", "బలాక్ష మౌద్గల్య", "శత", "శత-బలాక్ష మౌద్గల్య"