tayātu", "yAtu", "Sata", "SatayAtu", "యాతు", "శత", "శత-యాతు", "శతయాతు", "ಯಾತು", "ಶತ", "ಶತ-ಯಾತು", "ಶತಯಾತು"]}], "sata-rudriya": [{"id": "Sata-rudriya", "headword": "शत-रुद्रिय", "headword_slp1": "Sata-rudriya", "fold": "sata-rudriya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Śata-rudriya, śata-rudrīya (hymn ‘relating to the hundred Rudras’), is the name of a section of the yajurveda, which celebrates the god rudra in his hundred aspects, enumerating his many epithets.\nFoot notes kāṭhaka Saṃhitā, xxi. 6; Satapatha brāhmaṇa, ix. 1, 1, 1; 2, 1; x. 1, 5, 3. 15.\ntaittirīya Saṃhitā, v. 4, 3, 1; 5, 9, 4; 7, 3, 3; taittirīya brāhmaṇa, iii. 11, 9, 9, etc.\ntaittirīya Saṃhitā, iv. 5, 1-11; kāṭhaka Saṃhitā, xvii. 11-16; Maitrāyaṇī Saṃhitā, ii. 9, 1 et seq.; Vājasaneyi Saṃhitā, xvi. 1 et seq.\nCf. Zimmer, Altindisches Leben, 202; Weber, Indian Literature, 108, 111, 159, 169, 170; Eggeling, Sacred Books of the East, 43, 150 et seq.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["rudriya", "shata", "shata-rudriya", "shatarudriya", "śata", "śata-rudriya", "śatarudriya", "रुद्रिय", "शत", "शतरुद्रिय", "రుద్రియ", "శత", "శత-రుద్రియ", "శతరుద్రియ", "ರುದ್ರಿಯ", "ಶತ", "ಶತ-ರುದ್ರಿಯ", "ಶತರುದ್ರಿಯ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["rudriya", "shata", "shata-rudriya", "shatarudriya", "śata", "śata-rudriya", "śatarudriya", "rudriya", "Sata", "Satarudriya", "రుద్రియ", "శత", "శత-రుద్రియ", "శతరుద్రియ", "ರುದ್ರಿಯ", "ಶತ", "ಶತ-ರುದ್ರಿಯ", "ಶತರುದ್ರಿಯ"]}], "sata-sarada": [{"id": "Sata-SArada", "headword": "शत-शारद", "headword_slp1": "Sata-SArada", "fold": "sata-sarada", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Śata-śārada in the Rigveda and the Atharvaveda denotes a ‘period of a hundred autumns’ or years.\nFoot notes vii. 101, 6; x. 161, 2.\ni. 35, 1; viii. 2, 2; 5, 21.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["shaarada", "shata", "shata-shaarada", "shatashaarada", "śata", "śata-śārada", "śataśārada", "śārada", "शत", "शतशारद", "श